tured a completely new format for Olympic sailing. All the boats raced six fleet races, with the top six finishers advancing to the second round, which was raced as a round-robin of match races. The top four boats then advanced to the semi-finals, where single-elimination match racing determined the medalists."] "\n\n" [:p {} "In the round-robin the Americans led with four wins and one loss, followed by Denmark, with three wins and two losses. Those two boats had also been 1-2 in the fleet racing. Germany and Great Britain were the other two crews moving on to the semi-finals. Chalk held in the semis as both the US and Denmark won their matches, 2-0. The favored Americans, however, lost two straight races in the final, as Denmark won the gold medal. Great Britain defeated Germany, 2-1, in the bronze medal races. " [:a {:href "/athletes/61235"} "Jesper Bank"] ", the Danish skipper, had won a bronze medal in Soling in 1988 and would return in 2000 and add a second gold medal."] "\n"] [:table {:class "table table-striped"} [:thead {} [:tr {} [:th {} "Pos"] [:th {} "Competitors"] [:th {} "NOC"] [:th {}] [:th {}] [:th {}]]] [:tbody {} [:tr {:class "", :style ""} [:td {} "1"] [:td {} "Denmark"] [:td {} [:a {:href "/countries/DEN"} [:img {:style "padding-right: 2px; vertical-align: middle", :src "https://olympedia-flags.s3.eu-central-1.amazonaws.com/DEN.png"}] "DEN"]] [:td {} [:span {:class "Gold"} "Gold"]] [:td {}] [:td {}]] [:tr {:class "", :style ""} [:td {}] [:td {:colspan "8"} [:a {:href "/athletes/61235"} "Jesper Bank"] " • " [:a {:href "/athletes/63616"} "Jesper Seier"] " • " [:a {:href "/athletes/63611"} "Steen Secher"]]] [:tr {:class "", :style ""} [:td {} "2"] [:td {} "United States"] [:td {} [:a {:href "/countries/USA"} [:img {:style "padding-right: 2px; vertical-align: middle", :src "https://olympedia-flags.s3.eu-central-1.amazonaws.com/USA.png"}] "USA"]] [:td {} [:span {:class "Silver"} "Silver"]] [:td {}] [:td {}]] [:tr {:class "", :style ""} [:td {}] [:td {: